<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">House of Clare</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as de Clare family</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Clares were an Anglo-Norman noble family named after Clare in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/suffolk">Suffolk</a>, among the wealthiest in medieval <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a>. They became earls of Hertford and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gloucester">Gloucester</a>, held the marcher lordship of Glamorgan from 1217 and built <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caerphilly-castle">Caerphilly Castle</a>, while a branch led the invasion of Ireland under Richard de Clare, '<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/richard-de-clare-2nd-earl-of-pembroke">Strongbow</a>'. The main line ended when <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/humphrey-gilbert">Gilbert</a> de Clare was killed at Bannockburn in 1314.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/house-of-clare.jpg" alt="House of Clare" width="320" height="352" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: AlexD · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:CoA_Gilbert_de_Clare.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
